<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Export options for `xcodebuild -exportArchive` (plan §15.2). Used by
  scripts/release.sh; there is no reason to run xcodebuild against this by hand.

  method = developer-id
      Sentry is distributed outside the Mac App Store and always will be. It
      reads private IOKit surfaces (libIOReport.dylib, IOHIDEventSystemClient)
      that do not exist inside the App Sandbox, and the App Store requires the
      sandbox — so `app-store` is not a method we are declining to use, it is a
      method that cannot produce a working build of this app. See
      Sentry/Sentry.entitlements and plan §14.1.

  destination = export
      Write the exported .app to disk and stop. The alternative, `upload`, hands
      the archive to Xcode's own notarization pipeline. We want the artifact on
      disk so it can go into a DMG first and be notarized as the DMG — that is
      what makes the ticket staple-able onto the thing users actually download.

  signingStyle = manual, signingCertificate = Developer ID Application
      Matches CODE_SIGN_STYLE/CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY in project.yml's
      `DeveloperIDSigned` target template. Automatic signing would let Xcode
      pick an identity; on a machine that also has Apple Development certs for
      the iOS targets, "pick one" is not a decision worth delegating.

  No `provisioningProfiles` key, on purpose.
      A Developer ID export only needs a profile when the app claims an
      entitlement that must be authorized by one — App Groups, iCloud
      containers, push. This app claims none of those (again: see
      Sentry.entitlements, which is one key long and explains every absence).
      Adding an empty or speculative profile mapping here would introduce a
      moving part that expires annually in exchange for nothing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>method</key>
	<string>developer-id</string>
	<key>destination</key>
	<string>export</string>
	<key>teamID</key>
	<string>H7T2D2GL7U</string>
	<key>signingStyle</key>
	<string>manual</string>
	<key>signingCertificate</key>
	<string>Developer ID Application</string>
</dict>
</plist>
